course: dictionary
lesson: 76
title: Acrostic poems
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An acrostic is a poem or puzzle where the first letters of each line, read downwards, spell a word. That word is often the subject of the poem. «An acrostic poem spells a word with the first letter of each line, and each line should be a phrase, not just one word.» So for SPRING, you write S, P, R, I, N, G down the side and start each line with one of those letters.
explain: Each line should be a phrase, not just one word. For SUN you could write "Shining over the fields", "Underneath the blue sky", and "Nothing can hide from its light". Each line builds a little picture or idea.
explain: An acrostic can also be a word puzzle built the same way. You write a hidden word down the side, then give a clue for each line that starts with its letter.
explain: Other poems work differently. A kenning names a thing with two-word phrases, and a shape poem is laid out in the shape of its subject. An acrostic's message is in the first letters, read down.
fact: An acrostic is a poem or puzzle in which the first letters of each line, read downwards, spell a word.
fact: The word spelled out is often the subject of the poem, such as SPRING or a person's name.
fact: «An acrostic poem» means a poem where the first letters of the lines spell a word.
fact: Each line of an acrostic should be a phrase, not just one word.
fact: Acrostic is a noun (an acrostic, acrostics), and it can also work as an adjective, as in «an acrostic for your name».
exercise: In an acrostic poem for SPRING, which letter must the third line start with? | G | P | *R | S
exercise: Which line is the best one for an acrostic about SUN? | Hot | Sunny sun sun | *Shining warmly over the fields | Sun
exercise: Find and copy the word for a poem where the first letters of each line spell a word. | shape poem | *acrostic | kenning | sentence
test: In an acrostic for the word RAIN, which letter does the second line start with? | I | R | *A | N
test: Which of these is a phrase, as an acrostic line should be? | Flowers | Bright | *Lovely lilies by the lake | Lake
exam: Which statement about acrostics is true? | They are always written in Hebrew | *The first letters of each line, read downwards, spell a word | They always rhyme at the end of each line | Each line must be only one word long
